<!--
  Jingle Bells
  Chorus. James Lord Pierpont (1857). Public domain.
  C major, 4/4, quarter = 120, 16 bars (32 s). Right hand: the melody, C4-G4.
  Left hand: roots C3 D3 F3 G3, one per bar. Every note is in C3-B4.

  bar | right hand     | left hand | words
    1 | E4 E4 E4       | C3        | Jin-gle bells,
    2 | E4 E4 E4       | C3        | jin-gle bells,
    3 | E4 G4 C4 D4    | C3        | jin-gle all the
    4 | E4             | C3        | way!
    5 | F4 F4 F4 F4    | F3        | Oh, what fun it
    6 | F4 E4 E4 E4 E4 | C3        | is to ride in a
    7 | E4 D4 D4 E4    | D3        | one-horse o-pen
    8 | D4 G4          | G3        | sleigh, hey!
    9 | E4 E4 E4       | C3        | Jin-gle bells,
   10 | E4 E4 E4       | C3        | jin-gle bells,
   11 | E4 G4 C4 D4    | C3        | jin-gle all the
   12 | E4             | C3        | way!
   13 | F4 F4 F4 F4    | F3        | Oh, what fun it
   14 | F4 E4 E4 E4 E4 | C3        | is to ride in a
   15 | G4 G4 F4 D4    | G3        | one-horse o-pen
   16 | C4             | C3        | sleigh!
-->
